WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
- Christina, so nice to see you.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.390
I'm sorry I'm not Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:04.530
- It's okay. It's fine.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.363
You're not bad.

00:00:05.363 --> 00:00:06.320
- Oh, thank you very much.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.774
I'll take it, I'll take it.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.330
Happy belated birthday.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.163
- [Christina] Thank you.

00:00:10.163 --> 00:00:10.996
- You just had it recently, right?

00:00:10.996 --> 00:00:12.000
(crowd cheering)

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.988
What'd you do to celebrate?

00:00:12.988 --> 00:00:15.990
- So I took my first solo trip.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.230
I went to Santorini, Greece,
London, Paris and Lisbon.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.406
- Whoa. Wait a minute you did,

00:00:21.406 --> 00:00:23.760
that's a big trip, you did that solo, huh?

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.593
- [Christina] Yeah.

00:00:24.593 --> 00:00:25.426
- [Mario] Wow.

00:00:25.426 --> 00:00:26.310
- [Christina] Yeah.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.450
- [Mario] Well, there you are right there

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.904
with the solo selfies and everything.

00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:30.360
What prompted that?

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.520
That's a very eat, prey, love
kind of move right there.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.350
- That's exactly what it was.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.960
I had been wanting to get
to Greece since I was 33

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.520
but then the pandemic happened

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.770
and I've been working so much.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.930
I've done, you know, two
TV shows, two movies.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.930
And when I finally got
some time, it was like

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.670
okay, I'm gonna go to Santorini and

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.520
I found the perfect place to go to.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.421
I got a little villa,

00:00:51.421 --> 00:00:54.861
and once I was in Greece, I was like okay,

00:00:54.861 --> 00:00:57.120
I'm gonna go to London for dinner.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.570
And then I went and met
some friends in Paris,

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.403
- [Mario] Look at that.

00:01:00.403 --> 00:01:01.920
- And then my last place was Lisbon.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.300
I just wanted, I've always wanted to go.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.315
- Look at that.

00:01:04.315 --> 00:01:05.148
(audience clapping)

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:05.981
That's so impressive.

00:01:05.981 --> 00:01:07.151
- Yeah.

00:01:07.151 --> 00:01:07.984
- That's so empowering.

00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:09.030
I can't even go to the movies by myself.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.220
And you went to the whole
that like, so many people-

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.020
- You, but like, do you need someone to be

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:13.890
in the movie theater with you?

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:14.723
You don't.

00:01:14.723 --> 00:01:15.556
- You don't.

00:01:15.556 --> 00:01:17.163
But I just like get mad lonely.

00:01:18.293 --> 00:01:19.126
- Okay.

00:01:19.126 --> 00:01:19.959
- You know what I'm saying?

00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:20.792
I like how, but that's so,

00:01:20.792 --> 00:01:22.710
that is a really cool thing to do.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.290
- I'm not gonna, I was, I
don't wanna say terrified,

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:26.220
that's not the word.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.840
But I mean, it is weird

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.340
like just being out by yourself so like,

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.510
you know obviously be safe.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.343
- [Mario] Sure

00:01:31.343 --> 00:01:32.610
- You know, check reviews and all of that.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:33.443
But I mean-

00:01:33.443 --> 00:01:34.276
- That's exciting too.

00:01:34.276 --> 00:01:35.310
- Yeah. But now that I finally did it,

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.840
it's like, okay, where else can I go?

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:37.673
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:37.673 --> 00:01:38.506
Okay. Okay.

00:01:38.506 --> 00:01:40.860
Now I know you're
originally from New Jersey

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:41.760
and I'm assuming that's where you got

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.593
your start in acting.

00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:44.460
- Yes. I grew up in a neighborhood

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.990
where there wasn't much to do.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.965
I had very busy parents and

00:01:47.965 --> 00:01:52.030
one day I was sneaking and
taking the elevator at school.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.940
And this woman, she looked at me

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:57.446
and she was like: hey kid,
you wanna join our club?

00:01:57.446 --> 00:01:58.950
And I was like, what club?

00:01:58.950 --> 00:01:59.970
And she's like, the drama club.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.533
And I said, okay.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:03.720
I joined it.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.949
She put me in her play
Grease, I played Frenchie.

00:02:07.949 --> 00:02:09.075
- Oh, good part.

00:02:09.075 --> 00:02:10.440
- And I was very unprepared.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.820
I didn't, I was so nervous,

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.500
that I couldn't remember any of my lines

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.560
and she just was yelling
them to me from the wing.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.720
And I felt so guilty about that

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.300
that I vowed that I would
never forget another line.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.603
The next play she put me in
was Annie and I was Annie.

00:02:23.603 --> 00:02:24.498
- Ooh, look at that.

00:02:24.498 --> 00:02:26.107
Major step up there.

00:02:26.107 --> 00:02:27.536
(crowd cheering)

00:02:27.536 --> 00:02:30.535
Did the teacher continue
to to follow your career?

00:02:30.535 --> 00:02:31.368
- Yes.

00:02:31.368 --> 00:02:32.280
- And have y'all spoke since?

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.350
- So she has since passed

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.240
but when I graduated high school

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.390
she started my fan club.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.513
- [Mario] Oh look at that.

00:02:40.513 --> 00:02:43.500
- And she used to send me
checks to get to auditions.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.333
- Oh. She's-

00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:46.230
- None of which I ever
cashed, but I still have 'em.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.870
And it just was her little
way of like just helping me.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.840
And it wasn't much, but it was
the sentiment that mattered.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:52.673
- So sweet,

00:02:52.673 --> 00:02:54.780
that's a perfect example of
how important teachers are.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.160
They really are, they
can be life changing.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:56.993
- Yeah.

00:02:56.993 --> 00:02:58.500
- So and cut to, you got a new movie.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.333
- Yeah.

00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:00.803
- Devotion, it's based on a true story.

00:03:00.803 --> 00:03:01.636
(crowd cheering)

00:03:01.636 --> 00:03:04.080
Whenever a movie starts
off with the thing,

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:04.913
based on a true story,

00:03:04.913 --> 00:03:06.480
I'm like, ooh, I'm hooked right there.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.890
And in this one you play the wife

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.170
of a fighter pilot in the Korean War.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.003
- Yes.

00:03:11.003 --> 00:03:12.150
- Right. Did you have an opportunity to,

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.050
to meet the family?

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:13.883
- I did.

00:03:13.883 --> 00:03:16.560
I play Daisy Brown and she is the wife of

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.570
Jessie Brown, Ensign Jesse Brown,

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:21.210
who is the first black naval aviator.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:26.210
And you know, he, what his role

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.590
in the Korean War was, was 70 years ago.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.090
So he's no longer here,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.590
Daisy's no longer here.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.870
And so kind of the
vanguards of the family are

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.310
her granddaughter and her daughter.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.040
And you know, just in talking to them

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.810
and this being a true story,

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.400
even though they're not here anymore

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.230
you still want to honor them

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.460
and you wanna do the best that you can.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.830
So it's just listening to the family

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.720
and you know, listening to the stories

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.300
and listening to just how much

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.490
Jessie loved Daisy and Daisy loved Jessie.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:57.510
And you know, I think
in telling this story

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.320
people will see like a
really beautiful example

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.230
of just black love
between these two people

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.180
in the midst of all of this adversity.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.257
It's the 1950s and you don't really see

00:04:09.257 --> 00:04:13.020
real conversations
between couples back then.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.210
So I'm really happy that we
got to do it in this film.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.050
So yeah.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:16.883
- That's beautiful.

00:04:16.883 --> 00:04:17.880
I'm looking forward to
seeing that on screen.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:18.713
- Thank you.

